# Your own capsule messages. These are supposed to be secret until 2047 and this repo is public —
# committing them would publish the thing the entire site promises not to publish.
my-messages.txt
my-messages*.txt
!my-messages.example.txt

# The exported archive. capsule-sealed.json.enc is every sealed message, encrypted — the encryption
# is the protection, but publishing the ciphertext to a public repo is free exposure and permanent
# in git history. It also puts the archive in the same place as everything else, which is exactly
# what the backup advice says not to do. The manifests are safe to publish, but they are generated
# output and belong wherever you choose to publish them, not in the source tree.
capsule-archive/
